4803818,-0.01614754,0.08143451,0.00105834,-0.24374917,0.00723458,-0.02367217,0.0092035,-0.07499265,-0.03484958,0.01630578,-0.06898207,-0.02663903,0.00073201,0.0179005,0.00878568,0.05763998,-0.01223543,0.04197263,0.02009252,0.00284601,-0.05805558,0.06112513,-0.00831408,-0.01238304,0.04226423,0.18436264,0.0722721,0.04111695,0.02194984,-0.01385054,0.06600582,0.00175115,-0.01606248,0.01389127,0.00458911,0.06850544,-0.02910766,0.03196299,0.00282558,-0.0281059,0.01376671,0.03110133,0.01178028,-0.01378779,0.01755895,-0.03985777,-0.03397075,0.1043044,-0.01111946,-0.04752782,-0.00497961,-0.00949792,0.05134354,0.0335005,-0.01458627,0.03111603,-0.00584556,0.04154505,0.02142733,0.00258191,-0.03336502,-0.03490346,0.00630676,0.03233254,0.00231815,0.00851359,0.0517212,-0.04969382],"last_embed":{"tokens":464,"hash":"j39423"}}},"last_read":{"hash":"j39423","at":1785687442643},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1785180583927,"size":19819,"at":1785677924972,"hash":"j39423"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,10],"##Over the past two months, I’ve used Claude + Microsoft’s Power BI Modeling MCP server (currently in public preview) on three real client engagements — a manufacturing distributor, a pharma supply chain client, and a financial services firm. Three different industries. Three different model maturities. Three very different findings. One was a genuine catch I would have missed in a manual audit. One was a false positive that pointed at a real issue elsewhere. One was simply faster validation of work I’d already done. Here’s what actually happened, what each finding teaches about how to use AI in BI workflows responsibly, and the honest disclosures about how I ran these without exposing client data.":[11,16],"##Over the past two months, I’ve used Claude + Microsoft’s Power BI Modeling MCP server (currently in public preview) on three real client engagements — a manufacturing distributor, a pharma supply chain client, and a financial services firm. Three different industries. Three different model maturities. Three very different findings. One was a genuine catch I would have missed in a manual audit. One was a false positive that pointed at a real issue elsewhere. One was simply faster validation of work I’d already done. Here’s what actually happened, what each finding teaches about how to use AI in BI workflows responsibly, and the honest disclosures about how I ran these without exposing client data.#{1}":[13,16],"##First, The Trust Disclosures (Because They Matter)":[17,34],"##First, The Trust Disclosures (Because They Matter)#{1}":[19,34],"##Client 1: The Manufacturing Distributor (A Real Catch)":[35,62],"##Client 1: The Manufacturing Distributor (A Real Catch)#{1}":[37,62],"##Client 2: The Pharma Supply Chain Client (A False Positive That Revealed Something)":[63,88],"##Client 2: The Pharma Supply Chain Client (A False Positive That Revealed Something)#{1}":[65,88],"##Client 3: The Financial Services Firm (Faster Validation, Not New Findings)":[89,112],"##Client 3: The Financial Services Firm (Faster Validation, Not New Findings)#{1}":[91,112],"##The Honest Scorecard Across Three Clients":[113,122],"##The Honest Scorecard Across Three Clients#{1}":[115,122],"##What I’m Now Comfortable Saying About Claude + MCP for Real BI Work":[123,136],"##What I’m Now Comfortable Saying About Claude + MCP for Real BI Work#{1}":[125,136],"##What I’d Tell Someone Considering This For Their Own Models":[137,150],"##What I’d Tell Someone Considering This For Their Own Models#{1}":[139,150],"##The Bigger Picture (Same Picture From Different Angles)":[151,173],"##The Bigger Picture (Same Picture From Different Angles)#{1}":[153,173]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Gulab Chand Tejwani","target":"Gulab Chand Tejwani","line":5}],"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"key":"99.System/InboxArchive/2026-08/I Connected Claude to 3 Real Client Power BI Models Via MCP. Here's What It Caught - and What It Got Wrong.md"},
